      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1,700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is double the usual maximum for metformin.\n\n- **Maximum dose:** The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. For extended-release it is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. They add no glycemic benefit, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg/day total, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily (2,000 mg/day)\n- Another dose\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
